Z||000002||sdm1964||10-26-2000||06:58 AM||||They either say nice car, Don't see many of those any more. Or they break there necks trying to figure out what kida car it is. Then when they find out it it is fiero they don't those catch on fire? Then i give them one of these :rolleyes. Our own crowd||||reg||12
Z||000003||ChadMan||10-26-2000||08:16 AM||||I think we're in with the sportscar world, but we're the black sheep of the family.||||reg||9
Z||000004||elfiero||10-26-2000||09:33 AM||||God knows i love fieros(got three)but many<BR>people think of us as video game playing<BR>trekkie techno geeks.I know this is not true<BR>and so do the rest of you,but this is what most people perceive us to be.Throw in the<BR>bad press and GM's hate for the car,and you<BR>get a bunch of lonely guys that nobody likes.||||reg||6
Z||000005||DaRkLoRD||10-26-2000||10:09 AM||||one of my friends spent the latter half of high school dissing the fiero, big time.. then he saw a red 88 GT, and didn't believe me when I said it was a Fiero.. then he said it <B>must</B> be a body kit.. and I said no, that's what the fastback GT looks like!!<P>a couple of months later he went for a ride in an 87 GT.. now he's in the process of getting financing to buy one.. LOL.<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||10
Z||000006||Tigger||10-26-2000||10:27 AM||||I really hate to say it but at this time, we're in a crowd of our own.  Too many people are cluster phobic, and a heck of a whole lot of people are overweight up here.  The combination doesn't go so well for a small sportscar.<P>The big push for trucks and SUV's as "status symbols" doesn't help.  And the "myths" about our cars just adds to the confusion.  Lots of people I talk to and never owned a small car seem to have the "small car = death trap" complex.  I probably should remind them that NO car is completely safe, and I'm sure many of us here have some first hand knowledge of how exactly safe our Fiero's really are.<P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerblue.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||2xsess||10-26-2000||10:42 AM||||Who cares, I have fun driving my little coffin on wheels!!!<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||1
Z||000008||Cheever2||10-26-2000||11:30 AM||||I think a sign of the times is people are skeptical of everything.  With all the scams, low-quality stuff hyped for quick sale, and elected leaders we talk endlessly about then prove they're nothing but a joke, (where was I - oh yeah)... people have to be wary and not take anything at face value.  The Show-Me state should consider changing its motto to Oh Yeah? Prove It To Me.  The wildest crap ever now seems to be daily news, and what used to be a shocking movie is cartoonish compared to what they're making now (you can't even scare people anymore).  <BR>My point is people either gotta drive something for themselves, or get info from trusted friends, before they'll accept a car that was only made 5 years.  They're not just going to take our word for it that it's a fun sporty exciting great car.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||frontal lobe||10-26-2000||12:19 PM||||It's off most people's radar screens.  If you have a ton of money, you get a corvette.  If you have less money but want big horsepower, you get a firebird, camaro, or mustang.  If you want a foreign car, well...    But if you want a relatively inexpensive (at least to purchase), relatively light weight, sporty handling car with a reasonable power-to-weight ratio that at this price isn't a total rust-bucket and with surprisingly decent room inside and crash-worthiness, well what else is there left ON the radar screen?<P>So you have to be a bit of a contrarion, or at least a pretty individual thinker...which explains why the people on the forum are so interesting.  So there will be the masses that just "don't get it".  I can live with that.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Philphine||10-26-2000||12:26 PM||||it's (they're) mine and thats about all i can say about it. <P>------------------<BR>Phil T<P>'87 coupe (feral)<BR>'84 indy<BR>'84 coupe (cheap thrill)<p>[This message has been edited by Philphine (edited 10-26-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||Raydar||10-26-2000||12:28 PM||||Most annoying description that I've heard is "redneck Ferrari wannabe". <BR>The thing is, I never thought of a Fiero as a Ferrari wannabe. Not even close. I always thought of it as a cool little sports car. Good competition for the MR-2 and the Miata. Later on, I thought that it could have been a serious challenge to the Corvette, given another three years of development.  <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.||||reg||8
Z||000012||Zorba||10-26-2000||12:52 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Raydar:<BR><B>Most annoying description that I've heard is "redneck Ferrari wannabeears of development.  <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That's why it is so much fun to kick their a** on the road with a v8 fiero or ferrari body kit...all of a sudden...they don't have the same opinion again. nOthing like a sleeper with 400hp underneath and light weight.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000013||DavidHenshaw||10-26-2000||09:54 PM||||Personally, I think its an individual thing. <P>I've always liked Porsche but had no use for Corvettes which I always thought of as cars pretending to be something they aren't. Until recent production years I would have said that all Corvettes were poor performers, high horsepower aside. <P>Ditto for all the muscle cars including Cameros and Firebirds. So what if you have 300 horsepower. I want to know if a car can corner, brake and be graceful. OK, I'd rather own a nice Porsche but my 86 GT fastback is right up there in my opinion.<P>Dave||||reg||1
Z||000014||MrPBody||10-26-2000||09:59 PM||||Yep, "redneck ferrari wannabe" is about how my wife perceived Fiero until she drove it.  Now, she thinks it's pretty cool.<P>When I tell someone I own a Fiero, response usually falls into one of two groups:<P>    Mechanics and others with some technical knowledge say "That's an interesting car."<P>    Most other people curl their lips and go "Eeeeww, why would you buy one of those?"<P>Fiero has a rotten public image, but I have met only helpful and nice Fiero owners.  Maybe it's like the "good old days" (whenever those were) when anyone who drove a sports or foreign car was regarded as a bit looney.  We loonies  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> have to stick together.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000015||RobertVol||10-26-2000||10:37 PM||||I How are fieros perceived ??? hmmmm<P>Pretty well from behind my 3800 SC rear end!  <P>SEEEEEEEEE YAAAAAAAA!<P>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT Top 3.8 SC t top <BR>88GT 55k  <BR>North Florida Fiero Club <A HREF="http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros" TARGET=_blank>http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros</A>||||reg||1
Z||000016||Pontiaddict||10-26-2000||11:21 PM||||I don't get it either. A friend of mine (the one who nailed my '84) Doesn't like Fieros because he had to replace a motor and the  tranny twice on an '84 his dad had. Meanwhile, on the junk Bronco he owns he had gone through a tranny a week, a dozen rear ends, 3 or 4 transfer cases, 5 or 6 front ends, and a whole lot of other problems, but it was the best car (truck) he ever owned. The idiot that bought my '84 had done about a bazillion holeshots in parking lots with it, buried the speedometer in 3rd (5500rpms!), and then blames ME for the transmission not shifting right.<P>If a Fiero isn't a sports car when you get it, you just make it into one.||||reg||1
Z||000017||Raydar||10-27-2000||07:19 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Pontiaddict:<BR><B>...Meanwhile, on the junk Bronco he owns he had gone through a tranny a week, a dozen rear ends, 3 or 4 transfer cases, 5 or 6 front ends, and a whole lot of other problems,...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Sounds like one of those people who could tear up an iron anvil with a rubber hammer.<P><P>------------------<BR>Raydar<P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.||||reg||1
Z||000018||RaeQwan||10-27-2000||09:43 PM||||About Fiero owners being Video Game playing, trekkie geeks.. let be disect this... <P>Me.. Video Game player.. Yes very much..<BR>Me.. Trekkie nutt.. very much so, love star trek.<BR>Me. Geek.. In ya'lls minds, I own a fiero? am I a geek?<P>Crazy I may be, I'll not argue that fact. but when someone asks me why I bought my 88.. answers rather simple, cuz I wanted to. cuz its the car I wanted. plus from my experince.. its a babe magnet round this lil town... Aint found a woman yet that hasn't LOVED my 88. <P>So what do I say when ppl put my car down, talk badly bout it. nothing, cuz its my car. not theirs.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/raeqwanpenguin.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000019||88formula||10-27-2000||09:49 PM||||I perceive it as a gem in the rough.||||reg||1
Z||000020||Pontiaddict||10-27-2000||10:28 PM||||Raydar, his Bronco usually broke after tearing through a 6 pack. If ya know what I mean. It also explains why he likes it so much. The Fiero wasn't driven by him. Also, back in autoshop class, we were watching an old gm training video that had a fiero driving around in it (don't think it was being repaired) and he says, "Yeah, now watch it roll over and explode." And I go, "You mean like a jacked up Bronco?" I mean, How many cars that sit lower than a Corvette have you seen roll over?||||reg||1
